# Wave W17-AA (Route 218): cause rock — causeway footing rock: a jointed grey-brown boulder standing in bright harbour water, foam collar at its base where the planks’ feet meet the sea (design: the causeway’s footings stand in bright water the whole way). Route 218’s own rock — split from Route 219’s jetty rock by office entire (a footing that carries a road vs a jetty stone in open shallows) and from Foamline’s shallows rock by depth: harbour water here, bright shallows there.
